-  "Fix up TestExecutionEnvironment state: if our watchdog killed the test process,
-   the ensure: block in runTestCase: may not have fired, leaving testCompleted=false.
-   The env watchdog at P79 is blocked in waitTimeoutMilliseconds: — it won''t check
-   testCompleted until signaled or timed out. Signal only for timeouts."
-  result == #timeout ifTrue: [
-    [| env wds |
-     env := CurrentExecutionEnvironment value.
-     env instVarNamed: ''testCompleted'' put: true.
-     wds := env instVarNamed: ''watchDogSemaphore''.
-     wds ifNotNil: [wds signal]]
-    on: Error do: [:e |]].
+  "Stand the environment's watchdog down after EVERY test, not only after a
+   timeout.  This runner calls runCase, never runTestCase:, so nothing else sets
+   testCompleted.  A test that calls `self timeLimit: 30 seconds` (ProtoObjectTest,
+   IntegerTest, TraitFileOutTest, ...) runs TestCase>>timeLimit:, which signals the
+   watchdog; the watchdog then waits in 30 s slices with testCompleted still false
+   and, at the end of each slice, signals TestTookTooMuchTime into whatever test
+   process is running at that moment (hostEnv mainTestProcess).  Victims are
+   unrelated tests chosen by the wall clock, every 5-60 s until the batch ends.
+   Measured 2026-11-13 on Pharo 13 x86_64, batch 1951-2000: four victims 30 s
+   apart; with this block: none in 3 runs of batch 1-50 (4 of 4 without).
+   Also set testCompleted false at the start of each test (above), as
+   TestExecutionEnvironment>>runTestCase: does.
+   If our watchdog killed the test process, the ensure: block in runTestCase:
+   may not have fired either; the semaphore signal wakes the watchdog so it
+   reads testCompleted."
+  [| env wds |
+   env := CurrentExecutionEnvironment value.
+   env instVarNamed: ''testCompleted'' put: true.
+   wds := env instVarNamed: ''watchDogSemaphore''.
+   wds ifNotNil: [wds signal]]
+    on: Error do: [:e |].
 
   ^ result' classified: 'running'!
 
